  "id": "DrugBank_DB01042 - MONDO_8170",
  "verbalization": "Melphalan exhibits a strong association with Ovarian Cancer through a series of indication links, suggesting a potential role in its pathogenesis. The evidence indicates that Melphalan is linked to Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous and Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumors of the Ovary, both of which are classified as indications for Ovarian Cancer. This suggests that Melphalan may have a role in the development or progression of ovarian cancer, possibly through mechanisms involving the treatment of germ cell tumors. The presence of Tretamine as an intermediate in both pathways further implies a possible involvement in the biological processes that lead to ovarian cancer. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integrated evidence suggests that Melphalan may be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of ovarian cancer, particularly in cases involving germ cell tumors. The pathways highlight a potential dependency on certain molecular mechanisms, which could be explored for therapeutic applications.",
